// NEGATIVE: a non-defaulted param may NOT follow a defaulted one (1.8).
//
// The arity logic counts params with NO default, so `f(a, b = 5, c)` yields
// min_arity 2 and the call `f(1, 2)` passes the check -- but `2` binds POSITIONALLY
// to `b`, and `c` is padded with a fresh type var that no default can ever fill.
// Nothing rejected this. Python raises SyntaxError at def time; C++ rejects it at
// declaration. NOVA now fails closed at fn registration.
//
// A variadic rest param (`T...`) is deliberately still allowed in last position --
// it is legitimately optional and is handled by the variadic collapse, not by the
// default-padding path.

fn bad_order(a: int, b: int = 5, c: int) -> int
    a + b + c

fn main()
    print(str(bad_order(1, 2)))
